@startuml
title RuleSphere - Activity Diagram\n05. Promote, Rollback and Convergence | UC-18..20, UC-27
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #F0ECFF
skinparam activityBorderColor #496477

|Release Manager|
|Control / Delivery Plane|
|Runtime Node (Fleet)|
|Fleet Observability|
|Authorized Operator|

' Activity 1: Promotion or Rollback Trigger
|Release Manager|
start
:Request promote candidate or rollback to prior version;
|Control / Delivery Plane|
:Authorize operation and verify target eligibility;
if (Authorized and policy satisfied?) then (yes)
  :Switch desired Active pointer to target artifact;
  note right
    Rollback reuses an eligible prior immutable artifact.
    No cloning or rebuild needed.
  end note
  :Record actor, from/to version, timestamp and reason;
  :Emit desired-state publication event;
  :Acknowledge desired-state update to Release Manager;
else (no)
  :Return access / policy error;
endif
stop

' Activity 2: Concurrent Fleet Synchronization & Observability
|Control / Delivery Plane|
start
:Broadcast desired-state change event to Runtime fleet;
fork
  |Runtime Node (Fleet)|
  :Active Runtime nodes independently receive event;
  note right
    Concurrent execution across all active fleet nodes.
    Zero-restart in-memory load without interrupting in-flight requests.
  end note
  :Fetch exact immutable artifact and dependency references;
  :Verify checksum integrity and contract compatibility;
  if (Integrity and validation pass?) then (yes)
    :Load artifact into memory;
    :Mark snapshot eligible for new incoming requests;
    :Report loaded version, generation and healthy status;
  else (no)
    :Reject failed artifact;
    :Retain previously loaded valid artifact (FR-DIST-004);
    :Continue serving while emitting error alert;
  endif
fork again
  |Fleet Observability|
  :Track desired vs loaded status from all active nodes;
  if (100% of active nodes eligible within <=2.0s?) then (yes)
    :Mark fleet state as CONVERGED (NFR-CONS-001);
  else (no)
    :Expose convergence lag and alert SLA breach;
  endif
end fork
stop

' Activity 3: Independent Fleet Observation Query
|Authorized Operator|
start
:Request current fleet convergence status;
|Control / Delivery Plane|
:Authorize observation scope;
if (Authorized?) then (yes)
  :Query Fleet Observability collector;
  :Return node-by-node desired/loaded versions, lag, and errors;
  |Authorized Operator|
  :Inspect fleet convergence dashboard;
else (no)
  |Control / Delivery Plane|
  :Return access denied error;
endif
stop

legend bottom
  F-14 Resolution: Decoupled into Promotion/Rollback, Fleet Synchronization, and Operator Query.
  Fleet nodes synchronize concurrently with zero restart. Failed nodes retain valid loaded artifacts (FR-DIST-004).
  SLA is <=2.0s from event emission to 100% active nodes loaded and eligible (NFR-CONS-001).
endlegend
@enduml
